{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You shall not do so to YHWH your Elohim</b> — to burn incense to the heavens in every place, but only in the place that He shall choose. Another interpretation: \"And you shall tear down their altars and destroy their names — you shall not do so\" — this is a warning against erasing the Name and against tearing down even a single stone from the altar or from the courtyard. Rabbi Yishmael said: Would it even enter your mind that Israel tears down altars? Rather, that you should not do like their deeds and thereby cause the sins of your enemies to result in the destruction of the Temple of your fathers — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 12:4). But the words of Rabbi Yishmael are an admonition of aggadah, whereas the verse according to the opinion of our Sages is a warning against erasing the Name, as is explicitly stated in tractate Makkot (Makkot 22a): \"Now is there one who erases the Name for burning? And his warning is derived from here: 'You shall not do so to YHWH your Elohim.'\" And the language of the Sifrei (Sifrei Re'eh 7): \"From where do we learn that one who tears down a single stone [is liable]?… Rabbi Yishmael says: From where do we learn that one who erases a single letter from the Name transgresses a negative commandment, as it is stated: 'And you shall destroy their names — you shall not do so'? Rabban Gamliel son of Rabbi says: Would it even enter your mind…\" And the words of Rabbi Yishmael are not in dispute; rather, they are an explanation, for erasing the Name is like tearing down a stone from the altar. If so, the meaning of the verse is: \"And you shall tear down their altars and destroy their names from that place\" — but \"you shall not do so to YHWH your Elohim\" — to tear down His altar and destroy His Name; rather, you shall give honor to His Name and to His altar. And to the place that He shall choose to set His altar there for His Name, you shall seek, and you shall bring your burnt offerings before Him:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:48:47.420639970Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}